error[E0401]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), and a closure that uses it may be called more than once, or never
  --> resources_nested.ck:41:12
   |
41 | fn closure f -> r : f~File, r~Nat
   |            ^
   = note: a closure using `f` is passed to `twice`, whose parameter is not `own`, so `twice` may call it any number of times
   = help: mark that parameter of `twice` with `own` (as in `f~own (Unit -> a)`)

error[E0401]: `f` holds a resource (`File`), so it must be used exactly once, but `returned` may use it more than once
  --> resources_nested.ck:45:13
   |
45 | fn returned f -> r : f~File, r~File
   |             ^
   = note: `f` is passed to `same`, whose parameter is not `own`, so `same` may copy or drop it
   = help: mark that parameter of `same` with `own` (as in `x~own a`) so it can take a resource

